      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we first need to determine the total number of rounds played by all the golfers combined. We can do this by multiplying the number of rounds played by each group of golfers by the number of golfers in that group and then summing these products.\n\nThe chart provides the number of golfers in each group as well as the number of rounds played by each group:\n\n- 1 round of golf: 5 golfers\n- 2 rounds of golf: 2 golfers\n- 3 rounds of golf: 2 golfers\n- 4 rounds of golf: 3 golfers\n- 5 rounds of golf: 5 golfers\n\nWe can calculate the total number of rounds played as follows:\n\\[ (5 \\text{ golfers} \\times 1 \\text{ round}) + (2 \\text{ golfers} \\times 2 \\text{ rounds}) + (2 \\text{ golfers} \\times 3 \\text{ rounds}) + (3 \\text{ golfers} \\times 4 \\text{ rounds}) + (5 \\text{ golfers} \\times 5 \\text{ rounds}) \\]\n\nLet's compute this step-by-step:\n\\[ 5 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 + 2 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 5 \\]\n\\[ = 5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 \\]\n\\[ = 54 \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the total number of golfers by summing the number of golfers in each group:\n\\[ 5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 17 \\]\n\nNow, to find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we divide the total number of rounds played by the total number of golfers:\n\\[ \\text{Average number of rounds} = \\frac{54}{17} \\approx 3.1765 \\]\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\\[ \\boxed{3} \\]",
